From 50d98d36263cf38cd143b5897eab2adbdd937396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:27:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add voice search: mic button, remote hotkey, and fuzzy
 app-name matching

Adds a mic button to the home screen search bar that starts Android's
built-in speech recognizer (RecognizerIntent). A spoken phrase that
closely matches an installed app's name (Levenshtein-based fuzzy
match) launches that app directly; anything else falls back to a
normal typed search using the existing Search Results section.

- JoeTvNavigation gains a voiceSearchSignal so MainActivity can trigger
  voice search from the remote's search/assist/voice-assist button,
  the same way homeResetSignal handles the Home key.
- HomeScreen requests RECORD_AUDIO at runtime, launches the
  recognizer, and shows a full-screen "Listening..." overlay with a
  pulsing mic while it's active.
- AndroidManifest.xml: RECORD_AUDIO permission + a <queries> entry so
  JoeTV can resolve the system speech recognizer on Android 11+.

Not yet build-verified on device -- this container has no Android SDK
and can't reach dl.google.com to fetch one, so verification here was
limited to a brace/paren balance check and confirming every new
symbol (RecognizerIntent, ActivityResultContracts, ContextCompat,
etc.) is already imported and used elsewhere in these files. Needs a
real ./gradlew installDebug and an on-device test next.

